WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:08.990
Aura is a multi-national NASA scientific research satellite in orbit around the Earth, studying the Earth's ozone layer, air quality and climate.

00:09.470 --> 00:15.601
It is the third major component of the Earth Observing System (EOS) following on Terra and Aqua.

00:16.132 --> 00:20.488
Aura follows on from the Upper Atmosphere Research Satellite (UARS).

00:20.976 --> 00:25.116
Aura is a joint mission between NASA, the Netherlands, Finland, and the U.K.

00:25.776 --> 00:37.652
The Aura spacecraft is healthy and is expected to operate until at least 2028, possibly beyond, however only two of its four instruments are functioning nominally.
